# Frontend (Vue / JavaScript)

## Vue reactivity

- Use `reactive` instead of `ref` for objects and arrays wherever possible.
- Use `ref` only for primitives (booleans, strings, numbers) when needed.
- Use `computed` for reactive store access (e.g. `const user = computed(() => authStore.getUser)`).
- Use `ref` for DOM element references (e.g. `const fileInput = ref(null)`).

## Change markers (when editing existing files)

- Mark code changes with `✅ ADDED`, `✅ CHANGED`, `✅ REMOVED` indicators.

## API calls and error handling

- Use `async/await` for API calls.
- Always use `try` / `catch` / `finally` for error handling.
- Use `console.error()` for debugging errors.
- Update store state after successful API calls.
- Clear form data after successful submission.
- Use `router.push()` for navigation after successful actions.

## Loading states

- Use `setIsLoading(true/false)` in the store for loading state.
- Use `<Spinner :store="storeName" />` for loading indicators.
- Disable buttons during loading: `:disabled="store.isLoading"`.

## Toast notifications

- Use `toast.success()` for successful actions, `toast.error()` for errors, `toast.info()` for informational messages.
- Show toasts after API calls (success or error).

## File uploads

- Use `FormData` for file uploads.
- Set `enctype="multipart/form-data"` on the form element.
- Set `'Content-Type': 'multipart/form-data'` in axios headers.
- Clear the file input after a successful upload.

## Forms and validation display

- Use `@submit.prevent` for form submission.
- Use the `novalidate` attribute on forms to disable HTML5 validation.
- Clear validation errors on component mount (`onMounted`).
- Use `v-model` for two-way binding.
- Keep all validation logic on the Laravel backend (single source of truth); the frontend only displays backend validation errors.

## Component structure

- Use `<Spinner :store="storeName" />` for loading states.
- Use `<ValidationErrors :errors="errors" :visible="true/false" />` for error display.
- Clear validation errors and messages in `onMounted`.

## Styling

- Use Bootstrap utility classes (e.g. `mb-3`, `mt-2`, `d-flex`).
- Use Bootstrap Icons: `<i class="bi bi-icon-name"></i>`.
- Use `object-fit: cover` for images; use `rounded-circle` for profile images.
